cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this study's labels, corpus counts or results, cite the repository and tag retractionscope-v1-frozen."
title: "RetractionScope — Claim-Level Dependency on Retracted Papers: a measured study"
abstract: >-
  A frozen, measured study of claim-level dependency on retracted papers: which citing
  sentences actually rely on a retracted source, rather than merely citing it. Reports a
  4,928-paper corpus around 792 retracted sources with 6,117 citation contexts, a
  300-context human-labelled gold set (37 RELIES_ON), claim extraction audited at 96.5%
  precision, a cost cascade at -55.6% cost with 56.7% retention, and a staged detector
  that does not meet its pre-registered recall gate. The P3 gate is recorded as not passed.
authors:
